cfasl-1 — Binary fasl container format spec (plan-1-compact-fasl).

Design (no code) the on-disk format the serializer/loader implement.

CONTENT
- Header: 8-byte magic (e.g. "BOCLFAS\0"), u16 format-version, u16 flags, u32
  reserved.  A distinct magic from the text ";; BOCL <v> FASL" so LOAD can
  discriminate by peeking the first bytes.  file(1) friendliness: keep the magic
  ASCII-ish.
- Sections (offsets/lengths in the header, or streamed with section tags):
    1. INTERN TABLE: N entries, each = (package-name-string-index, symbol-name,
       flags[keyword/uninterned]).  Symbols in the object stream are referenced by
       their index here, so each is interned exactly once at load.
    2. CONSTANT POOL (optional): large/shared literals (strings, bignums, vectors)
       referenced by index, so duplicates are stored once.
    3. FORM STREAM: the serialized top-level forms, in order, each preceded by its
       byte length (for skip/validation).
- Value type tags for the object serializer (cons, nil, symbol-ref, small-int,
  bignum, ratio, single/double-float, character, string, simple-vector, structure,
  backref, T, package-designator, ...).  Reserve a tag space; version-gate.
- Endianness: fixed little-endian on disk (byte-swap on big-endian hosts) OR
  host-endian + a header endianness byte (simpler; document the choice).
- Versioning: LOAD checks format-version (major mismatch -> refuse/fall back to
  source, like %CHECK-FASL-VERSION does for the text fasl).

ACCEPTANCE: a written spec (this issue + a doc note) that cfasl-2 (writer) and
cfasl-3 (reader) can both implement unambiguously; agree the tag list.

DEPENDS ON: none (first).

== DONE (cfasl branch, v1.6.1) ==
The format spec is codified in sources/cfasl.h (magic "BOCLFASL" + u8 version +
u8 flags; the tag enum; the streaming shared-object model that subsumes the intern
table + constant pool and handles shared/circular structure; LEB128 varints and
little-endian floats for endianness-independence).  sources/cfasl.c implements the
low-level I/O the writer (cfasl-2) and loader (cfasl-3) build on: growable output
buffer, input cursor, u8/bytes, unsigned+signed (zig-zag) varints, little-endian
f32/f64.  Built into common_SRCS.  Round-trip test in test_misc "cfasl primitives".
DEVIATION from the sketch: chose a streaming incremental-id shared-object table
(simpler, handles cycles) over separate offset-based intern-table/constant-pool
sections.
